Students are expected to describe the characteristics of a balanced nutrition plan,
relevant to a client's sporting activity.

Students are expected, for each different client activity type provided, to show their
understanding of the differing dietary requirements of each of the activities.

Students should review the client's nutrition plan provided.  They should create a 2
week nutrition plan and then make amendments to this plan to make it suitable for
their client's sporting activity. The students will then need to provide an evaluation.

Students are expected to discuss the negative effects of an unbalanced nutrition plan as
well as the benefits of a manipulated nutrition plan.

