1589: 4.2  Unit R180: Reducing the risk of sports injuries and dealing with
1590: 
1591: common medical conditions
1592: 
1593: Aims
1594: 
1595: Taking part in sport and physical activity puts the body
1596: under stress. Sports injuries can be caused in many
1597: ways, ranging from accidental to deliberate acts of foul
1598: play. They can also depend on various extrinsic and
1599: intrinsic factors. Knowing how to reduce the risk of
1600: injury when taking part in sport, and how to respond
1601: to injuries in a sport setting are vital skills in many roles
1602: within the sport and leisure industry. Millions of people
1603: in the UK are suffering from medical conditions that
1604: may influence their participation in sport and physical
1605: activity, but with knowledge and understanding of
1606: 
1607: common medical conditions, along with the correct
1608: treatment and emergency procedures, more people
1609: can continue to participate in sporting activities in a
1610: safer environment.
1611: 
1612: In this unit you will learn how to prepare participants to
1613: take part in sport and physical activity in a way which
1614: minimises the risk of injuries occurring; prepare them to
1615: be able to respond to common injuries that can occur
1616: during sport and physical activity and to recognise the
1617: symptoms of some common medical conditions.
1618: 
1619: Unit R180: Reducing the risk of sports injuries and dealing with common medical
1620: conditions
